            <title><![CDATA[MAI Code 2 and Code 2 Flash (222 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://microsoft.ai/news/introducing-mai-code-2-and-mai-code-2-flash/</link>
            <guid>50535885</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:25:13 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://microsoft.ai/news/introducing-mai-code-2-and-mai-code-2-flash/">https://microsoft.ai/news/introducing-mai-code-2-and-mai-code-2-flash/</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50535885">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div data-block-component="wysiwyg">
        <h2>Performance and speed for everyday coding</h2>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">MAI Code 2 is at the frontier of price-performance for common enterprise coding tasks and excels in taking code to production, deep debugging, multi-file implementation, repo wide reasoning, and UI. It does all of this while also delivering changes code maintainers would merge, at a fraction of frontier cost. </span><span data-ccp-props="{}"> </span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">Meanwhile, MAI Code 2 Flash is designed for high-volume work such as code explanations, targeted edits, routine fixes, and rapid iterations, while bringing quality at a much lower cost. </span><span data-ccp-props="{}"> </span></p>
<h2>Production quality at less than half the price</h2>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">To deliver the best price-performance, we’ve built these models to prioritize the coding work our customers do every day. They’re explicitly not yet tuned for harder problems, like fundamental science research and very long horizon agentic work.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}"> </span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">Averaged over four widely used benchmarks that target the everyday enterprise coding tasks we see in GitHub Copilot (DeepSWE 1.1, Terminal Bench 2.1, SWE-Atlas and FrontierCode v1.1), MAI Code 2 gives you <b>98%</b> of the performance of GPT 6.1 Sol at <b>40%</b> of the cost, and </span><b><span data-contrast="auto">96% </span></b><span data-contrast="auto">of Claude Opus 5.5’s performance at just </span><b><span data-contrast="auto">5%</span></b><span data-contrast="auto"> of the cost.<sup><a href="#fn-1">1</a></sup></span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">MAI Code 2 is also tuned for producing great dashboards and visualizations, and excels at visual coding. In blind frontend app evaluations, reviewers preferred its results over GPT-6 Sol 67% of the time.<sup><a href="#fn-2">2</a></sup></span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">In addition, MAI Code 2 Flash offers comparable performance to GPT-6 Luna and Claude Haiku 5.5 at </span><b><span data-contrast="auto">6</span></b><b><span data-contrast="auto">5% </span></b><span data-contrast="auto">and </span><b><span data-contrast="auto">20%</span></b><span data-contrast="auto"> of the cost,</span><span data-contrast="auto"> across three coding benchmarks measuring day-to-day, high-volume routine coding tasks.<sup><a href="#fn-3">3</a></sup></span></p>
      </div></div>]]></description>
        </item>
