<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div><div><div><p>Published on:</p><p>Nov 17, 2026</p></div><div id="test" fs-toc-element="contents" fs-toc-offsettop="8rem"><h2>TL;DR</h2><ul role="list"><li>Java4Shell (CVE-2026-114938), a reported unauthenticated remote code execution flaw has been reported in Java 17, 21, 25 and 27 releases before the patched builds below, rated 9.2 under CVSS 4.0.</li><li>Oracle released patched builds on November 17, 2026. Java SE 8 and 11 are not affected by this CVE.</li><li>Update every Java line you run to the patched build in the table below,</li><li><strong>To find out if you are affected, click "Am I affected?" on </strong><a href="https://app.aikido.dev/dashboard" data-wf-native-id-path="2fc8390a-56f5-8c71-4985-68a0f08553da" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="2fc8390a-56f5-8c71-4985-68a0f08553da"><strong>the Aikido dashboard.</strong></a></li></ul><h2>Which Java versions and builds are affected?</h2><div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Product</th>
        <th>Affected version range</th>
        <th>Fixed version</th>
      </tr>
